1. Data connectivity modes
There 3 types of connectivity modes
1. Import mode
2. Direct mode
3. Composite mode

Import Mode : (we have access to download data)
→ Import mode is default method for developing Power BI desktop solutions and most commonly using method.

What are drawbacks of Import mode?
→ full refresh deletes all the data from the table and reload all the data from source. So it takes alot of time.

2. Direct mode:
→ In this mode the data is not imported into the model. instead they are simply metadata. Tht defines the model structure 

Q)when do we need to use the direct mode?
There are 3 reasons to use the direct mode 
1.	The company will not allow downloading the data but provide the access to read the data 
2.	When the data are too enormous to load into model  or practical refresh 
3.	When the reports and dashboards must give real-time  data that exceeds the constraints of scheduled refresh then we can use direct mode.

#what are disadvantages and drawback of direct mode?
Power query expression can only be works to native queries  that the data source understand

3.Composite Mode :  allows  you to combine both import and direct mode
